<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Chain Rule and Partial Derivatives _Nancy</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Given the following information</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle  w={@func_w@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle  x={@func_x@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle  y={@func_y@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle  z={@func_z@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle  p={@func_p@}\)</p>
<p> We can use Chain Rule to determine \( \displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{t}}\) and  \( \displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{s}}\) as follows; </p>
<p>First, let's find:</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{x}}=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]] </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle\frac{\partial{x}}{\partial{p}}= \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]] </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{p}}{\partial{t}}= \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]] </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{y}}= \) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]] </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{y}}{\partial{p}}=\) [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]] </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{y}}{\partial{t}}= \) [[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans6]] [[feedback:prt6]] </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{z}}=\) [[input:ans7]] [[validation:ans7]] [[feedback:prt7]] </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{t}}= \) [[input:ans8]] [[validation:ans8]] [[feedback:prt8]] </p>
<p> Then substitute them in the formulas below,</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{t}} = \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{x}}\frac{\partial{x}}{\partial{p}}\frac{d{p}}{d{t}}+ \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{y}}\frac{\partial{y}}{\partial{p}}\frac{d{p}}{d{t}}+  \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{y}}\frac{\partial{y}}{\partial{t}}+ \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{z}}\frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{t}}\)</p>
<p>\( \qquad =\)  [[input:ans9]] [[validation:ans9]] [[feedback:prt9]] </p>
<br>
<p>\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{s}}= \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{y}}\frac{\partial{y}}{\partial{s}}+\frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{z}}\frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{s}}\)</p>
<p>\(\qquad =\)  [[input:ans10]] [[validation:ans10]] [[feedback:prt10]] </p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b><h3>Worked solution</h3></b></p>
<p> We need to compute the partial derivates of the following functions as shown,</p>
\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{x}}= {@diff_wx@}\)
\(\displaystyle\frac{\partial{x}}{\partial{p}}= {@diff_xp@}\)
\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{p}}{\partial{t}}= {@diff_pt@}\)
\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{y}}= {@diff_wy@}\)
\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{y}}{\partial{p}}= {@diff_yp@}\)
\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{y}}{\partial{t}}= {@diff_yt@}\)
\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{z}}= {@diff_wz@}\)
\(\displaystyle \frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{t}}= {@diff_zt@}\)
<p> Then substitute them in the formulas below,</p>


\(\displaystyle 
\begin{align}
\displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{t}} & = \displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{x}}\frac{\partial{x}}{\partial{p}}\frac{\partial{p}}{\partial{t}}+ \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{y}}\frac{\partial{y}}{\partial{p}}\frac{\partial{p}}{\partial{t}}+  \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{y}}\frac{\partial{y}}{\partial{t}}+ \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{z}}\frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{t}}\\
& = \displaystyle {@ta1@}
\end{align}
\) </p>
<br>
<p>
\(\displaystyle 
\begin{align} 
\displaystyle \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{s}} & = \displaystyle  \frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{y}}\frac{\partial{y}}{\partial{s}}+\frac{\partial{w}}{\partial{z}}\frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{s}} \\
& = \displaystyle {@ta2@}
\end{align}\)</p>]]></text>
